---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CodeCard from '../components/CodeCard.astro';
import { mirrorBase, mirrorEntries, mirrorLive } from '../lib/mirror';

const entries = await mirrorEntries();
const fmt = (n?: number) => (n === undefined ? '-' : n.toLocaleString('en-GB'));
const chains: Record<number, string> = {
  1: 'Ethereum', 42161: 'Arbitrum One', 8453: 'Base', 56: 'BNB Chain', 137: 'Polygon',
  100: 'Gnosis', 10: 'Optimism', 143: 'Monad', 4663: 'Robinhood Chain',
};
const day = (iso?: string) => (iso ? iso.slice(0, 10) : '-');
const base = mirrorBase || 'https://mirror.nuthatch-indexer.com';
const seedCommand = (e: (typeof entries)[number]) => {
  const clone = e.repo.split('/').pop();
  const dir = e.path ? `${clone}/${e.path}` : clone;
  return `git clone ${e.repo}\n${e.commit ? `git -C ${clone} checkout ${e.commit.slice(0, 12)}\n` : ''}nuthatch seed --from ${base} --dir ${dir}
nuthatch dev --dir ${dir}${e.devArgs ? ` ${e.devArgs}` : ''}`;
};
// One real object, run against the bucket before this page shipped: 5,717 rows.
const readQuery = `SELECT count(*), min(block_number), max(block_number)
FROM read_parquet('${base}/494ce630fa704ee504e6cdfb8f732c66d585843face32fbbc6b7bf115a9b15c7/gns__subgraph_published/e03958df317ac9e39634669f04c7fc1c6e6caed29e7b5f37630235acd8c9f7f2.parquet');`;
---
<Layout
  path="/mirror"
  title="Public mirror - Nuthatch"
  description="Start a nest from indexed history someone has already paid for. Download a published mirror, check every file against its hash, and follow the chain from where it ends."
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="section-label">Mirror</p>
      <h1>Start from history, not from block zero</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A backfill is the expensive part of running a nest: about a million RPC credits for the Lodestar allocations
        nest (the 4.9.0 release notes), every one of them buying history somebody has already indexed. The public mirror
        holds that history. <code>nuthatch seed</code> downloads it, checks every file against its
        content address, and leaves your nest following the chain from the block where the mirror ends.
      </p>

      {!mirrorLive && (
        <p class="pending">
          The public bucket is not open yet. The nests below will be mirrored from the Lodestar
          deployment once it is, and this page fills in their figures at the next build.
        </p>
      )}

      <div class="how">
        <div class="steps">
          <div>
            <span class="cap">1 · the nest</span>
            <p>Clone the nest and check out the commit it was published from. The mirror is found by the nest's data identity, so any other version finds nothing.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="cap">2 · the history</span>
            <p>Seed downloads the sealed segments, refuses any file that does not hash to its address, and resumes if interrupted.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="cap">3 · the tip</span>
            <p>Dev follows the chain from the next block, over your own RPC. Seeding graph-gns-nest and catching up to the tip took six RPC calls (4.9.0 release notes).</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="grid">
        {entries.map((e) => (
          <li class="nest" id={`mirror-${e.nest}`}>
            <div class="nest-top">
              <h3>{e.nest}</h3>
              {e.completeThrough !== undefined ? (
                <span class="badge status--available">published {day(e.publishedAt)}</span>
              ) : (
                <span class="badge status--planned">{e.error ? 'unreadable' : 'not yet published'}</span>
              )}
            </div>

            {e.completeThrough !== undefined && (
              <dl class="figures">
                <div><dt>chain</dt><dd>{chains[e.chainId ?? 0] ?? e.chainId}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>history</dt><dd>{fmt(e.indexedFrom)} to {fmt(e.completeThrough)}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>rows</dt><dd>{fmt(e.rows)}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>files</dt><dd>{fmt(e.segments)} segments, {fmt(e.tables)} tables</dd></div>
              </dl>
            )}

            <div class="cmd">
              <CodeCard code={seedCommand(e)} lang="bash" label="shell" />
              <a class="repolink" href={e.repo} rel="noopener">{e.repo.replace('https://github.com/', '')} ↗</a>
            </div>
            {e.note && <p class="note">{e.note}</p>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div class="notes">
        <section>
          <h2>What the hashes prove</h2>
          <p>
            That every file is the one the mirror's catalogue names, so nothing changed on the way or at
            rest. They do not prove who wrote that catalogue, or that it is true to the chain. Seed from a mirror run by someone you
            would trust to run the nest for you, or re-index a sample of it yourself and compare.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Publish your own</h2>
          <p>
            Any nest can be a mirror. Run it with <code>--publish-target s3://your-bucket/prefix</code>, or
            run <code>nuthatch publish sync</code> on a stopped one, and point people at the bucket's public
            address. The mirror is append-only and costs nothing to read from a bucket that does not charge
            for downloads. The <a href="https://github.com/nuthatch-org/nuthatch/blob/main/docs/operators.md#data-lifecycle" rel="noopener">operator guide</a> has the bucket policy.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section class="read">
        <h2>Read it without Nuthatch</h2>
        <p>
          The mirror is plain Parquet, so DuckDB, Trino or anything else that reads Parquet over HTTPS can
          query it directly. A public bucket cannot be listed: each dataset's
          <code>manifest.json</code> names its tables and, for every segment, a <code>hash</code>, and the
          file is at <code>&lt;dataset&gt;/&lt;table&gt;/&lt;hash&gt;.parquet</code>. The manifest's
          <code>file</code> field is the name inside a nest directory, not the address here.
        </p>
        <CodeCard code={readQuery} lang="sql" label="duckdb" />
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .read { margin-top: 3rem; }
  .read h2 { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.2vw, 1.35rem); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .read p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: 72ch; }
  .page { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(4rem, 9vw, 6.5rem); }
  h1 { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .lede {
    color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 62ch;
  }
  code {
    background: var(--bg-inset); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 0.05rem 0.35rem; font-size: 0.85em;
  }
  .pending {
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 35%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 8%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.94rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .how {
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-elev); padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.2rem; }
  .steps p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .cap {
    display: block; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .grid {
    list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(22rem, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;
  }
  .nest {
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-elev); padding: 1.2rem 1.25rem 1.3rem;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; scroll-margin-top: 74px;
    transition: border-color 0.18s var(--ease);
  }
  .nest:hover { border-color: var(--border-hi); }
  .nest-top { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .nest-top h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .badge {
    flex-shrink: 0; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.64rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.18rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 9999px; border: 1px solid transparent;
  }
  .status--available { color: var(--ok); background: var(--pale-green-bg); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ok) 30%, transparent); }
  .status--planned { color: var(--text-faint); border-color: var(--border); }
  .figures { margin: 1rem 0 0; display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .figures div { display: flex; gap: 0.8rem; font-size: 0.86rem; }
  .figures dt {
    width: 4.5rem; flex-shrink: 0; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint); padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  .figures dd { margin: 0; color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .cmd { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 1.1rem; }
  .repolink {
    display: inline-block; margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .repolink:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .note { margin: 0.8rem 0 0; font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-faint); }
  .notes {
    margin-top: 3.5rem; display: grid; gap: 2rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(20rem, 1fr));
  }
  .notes h2 { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.2vw, 1.35rem); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .notes p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
</style>
